<body>
    <h1>AIP-186:  Enhanced Facial Recognition with Vision Models</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>Our current facial recognition system uses DeepFace as a common =
entry point for various face models (VGG-Face, ArcNet, etc.) and ChromaDB f=
or storing face embeddings and metadata. While functional, we identified se=
veral areas for improvement in training robustness and recognition accuracy=
.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Training process lacks robust validation</p></li>
<li>
<p>No quality-based filtering for training faces</p></li>
<li>
<p>Limited augmentation strategy</p></li>
<li>
<p>Fixed threshold approach for recognition</p></li>
<li>
<p>Limited temporal consistency in video processing</p></li>
<li>
<p>Basic face quality assessment</p></li>
</ol>
<p>We=E2=80=99ve been experimenting with whether we can integrate a Vision =
Model for validating training faces. See: <a class=3D"external-link" data-c=
ard-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://github.com/trezero/faceTools" rel=
=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/trezero/faceTools</a></p>
<p><strong>Advantages of Vision Model Integration:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Could detect subtle quality issues (partial occlusion, face masks, heavy=
 makeup)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Natural language feedback about image quality</p></li>
<li>
<p>Help ensure demographic diversity in training data</p></li>
<li>
<p>More nuanced understanding of edge cases</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Disadvantages of Vision Model Integration:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Significant latency overhead (100ms-2s per image)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Greatly increased system complexity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Resource management a concern.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-ComputerVision"=
><strong>Computer Vision </strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-ValidationPipel=
ine"><strong>Validation Pipeline</strong></h3>
<p>The validation pipeline uses multiple quality checks to ensure only high=
-quality faces proceed to training. Key validators include:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">class F=
aceValidator:
    def __init__(self):
        self.validators =3D [
            ResolutionValidator(min_size=3D(64, 64)),
            BrightnessValidator(min_brightness=3D0.3, max_brightness=3D0.9)=
,
            BlurValidator(max_blur=3D100),
            PoseValidator(max_angle=3D30),
            OcclusionValidator(max_occlusion=3D0.2)
        ]
       =20
    async def validate(self, face_image):
        results =3D [await validator.validate(face_image) for validator in =
self.validators]
        return ValidationResult(
            is_valid=3Dall(r.is_valid for r in results),
            details=3D{r.name: r.details for r in results}
        )
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>The pipeline validates resolution, brightness, contrast, blur, pose, and=
 occlusion, rejecting faces below the quality threshold.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-RecognitionPipe=
line"><strong>Recognition Pipeline</strong></h3>
<p>Adaptive Thresholding: Adjusts identification thresholds based on face q=
uality.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">def _ca=
lculate_adaptive_threshold(face_quality, distance):
    base_threshold =3D self.identification_threshold
    quality_factor =3D min(1.0, face_quality / self.optimal_quality_score)
    return base_threshold * quality_factor
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Temporal Smoothing: Ensures recognition consistency over time in video s=
treams.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">def _ap=
ply_temporal_smoothing(current_results, history):
    smoothed_results =3D []
    for result in current_results:
        historical_match =3D self._find_matching_face_in_history(result, hi=
story)
        smoothed_results.append(self._smooth_detection(result, historical_m=
atch))
    return smoothed_results
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-FaceQualityAsse=
ssment"><strong>Face Quality Assessment</strong></h3>
<p>The assessment combines metrics for resolution, brightness, and symmetry=
 into a weighted score:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">def ana=
lyze_face_quality(face_data, image):
    quality_scores =3D {
        'resolution': _calculate_face_resolution(face_data),
        'brightness': _analyze_brightness(image),
        'pose': _estimate_pose(face_data),
    }
    weighted_score =3D sum(
        score * QUALITY_WEIGHTS[metric]
        for metric, score in quality_scores.items()
    )
    return weighted_score
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-VisionModelInte=
gration"><strong>Vision Model Integration</strong></h2>
<p>Vision models provide natural language feedback and detect subtle qualit=
y issues like occlusion or heavy makeup. They complement traditional valida=
tors for borderline cases:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">class V=
isionModelValidator:
    def __init__(self, model_name=3D"gpt-4-vision-preview", confidence_thre=
shold=3D0.85):
        self.model =3D model_name
        self.confidence_threshold =3D confidence_threshold
       =20
    async def validate(self, image):
        response =3D await self._analyze_with_model(image)
        return self._parse_response(response)
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-VisionModelDete=
ction">Vision Model Detection</h3>
<p>While local vision models could supplement detection, we should not repl=
ace DeepFace's detection for a few reasons:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>DeepFace already abstracts several optimized detection backends:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>SSD (Single Shot Detector)</p></li>
<li>
<p>MTCNN (Multi-task Cascaded CNN)</p></li>
<li>
<p>RetinaFace</p></li>
<li>
<p>MediaPipe Face Detection</p></li>
<li>
<p>OpenCV's DNN face detector</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>These specialized detectors are optimized specifically for face detectio=
n and well-benchmarked on face detection datasets. They are orders of magni=
tude faster than general vision models and far more resource efficient</p>
<p>However, we could use the vision models to validate DeepFace's detection=
s:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">class E=
nhancedFaceDetector:
    def __init__(
        self,
        deepface_backend: str =3D "retinaface",
        vision_validator: Optional[LocalVisionValidator] =3D None
    ):
        self.detector =3D DeepFace.build_detector(detector_backend=3Ddeepfa=
ce_backend)
        self.vision_validator =3D vision_validator
       =20
    async def detect_faces(self, image: np.ndarray) -&gt; List[Dict]:
        # Get initial detections
        faces =3D self.detector.detect_faces(image)
       =20
        if self.vision_validator:
            # Validate each detection
            for face in faces:
                face_img =3D self._extract_face_region(image, face)
                validation =3D await self.vision_validator.validate(face_im=
g)
                face['confidence'] *=3D validation.confidence
               =20
        return [f for f in faces if f['confidence'] &gt; self.confidence_th=
reshold]</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>This would give us the best of both: specialized face detection with add=
itional validation from vision models.</p>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-Configuration">=
<strong>Configuration</strong></h2>
<p>The system=E2=80=99s behavior can be fine-tuned through several configur=
able settings:</p>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-QualitySettings=
"><strong>Quality Settings</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">quality=
_config =3D {
    'min_face_resolution': 64 * 64,
    'min_brightness': 0.3,
    'min_contrast': 0.4,
    'max_pose_angle': 30,
    'max_occlusion': 0.2
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-TemporalConfigu=
ration"><strong>Temporal Configuration</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">tempora=
l_config =3D {
    'history_size': 5,
    'smoothing_factor': 0.7,
    'min_track_length': 3
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-AugmentationSet=
tings"><strong>Augmentation Settings</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">augment=
ation_config =3D {
    'brightness_range': (-0.2, 0.2),
    'contrast_range': (-0.2, 0.2),
    'noise_range': (0, 0.05),
    'rotation_range': (-15, 15)
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-VisionModelConf=
iguration"><strong>Vision Model Configuration</strong></h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vision_=
config =3D {
    "enabled": False,
    "model": "gpt-4-vision-preview",
    "confidence_threshold": 0.85,
    "cache_size": 1000
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-VisualizationEx=
amples"><strong>Visualization Examples</strong></h3>
<h4 id=3D"AIP-186:EnhancedFacialRecognitionwithVisionModels-FaceQualityAnal=
ysis"><strong>Face Quality Analysis</strong></h4>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s an example output from the face quality analysis tool:</p=
>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"320eaac7-c7da-47ef-a058-e24=
8ddc12ce3" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Metric</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Score</p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p>Pass/Fail</p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Resolution</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>0.85</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Pass</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Brightness</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>0.78</p></td>
